            <ArticleTitle>[Pulmonary infiltrates and peripheral blood eosinophilia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 43-year-old asthmatic woman was hospitalised because of fever, cough, expectorations and asthenia. Chest X-rays showed bilateral pulmonary infiltrates. Peripheral blood eosinophilia was greater than 9 G/l. Bronchoalveolar lavage revealed a massive eosinophilia. The clinical features were consistent with a chronic eosinophilic pneumonia. All the symptoms resolved with the initiation of prednisone treatment. The differential diagnosis of eosinophilic pneumonia is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
